//! The skin package: a skeleton, the clips that pose it, and the mesh
//! that follows.
//!
//! `entelechy import` writes the rows out of a glTF and the Blender bridge
//! writes the same ones; what happens to them is Kernels, so a pose is
//! data the whole way and a scene can blend two clips, scrub one from
//! the pointer, or write a joint itself before the palette is made.
package skin@1 { language = 1; ir = 1; }

use "kernels/";
